{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "All That Echoes feels like a natural follow-up to Stages because expressive singing and melodic songs are a strong part of what I enjoy; Partners and Loved Me Back to Life also fit that polished vocal appeal.",
    "The Piano Guys connects with my latest relaxing classical listening through instrumental arrangements that suit a calm mood."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Closer To The Truth and Chronicle do not offer the orchestral vocal or calming instrumental experience I want today, even though I have listened to other popular music.",
    "The Book of Mormon shares a musical connection with my history, but its satirical character misses my relaxing mood; The Perfect Gift relates to earlier Christmas listening, but I am not seeking seasonal music now.",
    "Wynonna & The Big Noise has some connection to my country listening, but that connection is weaker than the vocal crossover choices; Hope gives me too little information to decide."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My earlier country and older pop listening seems to have been treated as a stronger guide to today's choices than it actually is.",
    "Having enjoyed Christmas music and musical performances does not mean I want any seasonal album or cast recording. The mood and style still matter."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent relaxing classical choice makes calm instrumental listening especially relevant right now.",
    "Across Stages, A Musical Affair, and Lead With Your Heart, the appeal for me is expressive, polished singing and melodic arrangements; a broad connection to popular music is less useful."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in expressive vocals and relaxing instruments, but stretched older listening interests beyond what I want today."
}"}
